## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/gamma.html
- Summary (EN): The Gamma node reshapes the tonal values of a layer, VDB, or attribute by applying an exponential gamma curve. It is commonly used for tone mapping, such as sRGB-style encoding with a value near 2.2, or for artistic adjustments.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Gamma corrige la courbe tonale d'une couche par une puissance exponentielle, pour l'encodage ou le décodage des couleurs.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: layer, VDB or attribute to correct", "gamma (optional): per-pixel gamma value multiplied with the Gamma parameter, then inverted if Invert is on", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask amount scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Mask: how much of the new value mixes with the original; default 1 uses only the new value", "Toggle RGB, Red, Green, Blue, Alpha: channels the effect applies to", "Gamma: correction factor; the default behavior is an encoding gamma that raises values to the inverse of the exponent", "Invert: switches between encoding and decoding gamma by inverting the exponent", "Treat RGBA as Premultiplied: un-premultiplies RGBA before correction and re-premultiplies afterward"]

- Caveats: ["With premultiplied RGBA layers, enable Treat RGBA as Premultiplied; leaving it off makes low-coverage areas look unexpectedly dark", "The page lists the output as gamma, which may be confusing when wiring downstream"]

